.TH PAVECLI 1 "" "PaveDB 0.9.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pavecli \- local PaveDB administration and data loading
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
pavecli [OPTION]... COMMAND [ARG]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
PaveDB CLI
.PP
Successful results go to stdout; service and file errors go to stderr as
JSON. Usage errors go to stderr with exit status 2. Use \- for stdin with
ingest\-batch and restore\-archive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Emit compact JSON for scripting
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version, copyright, and license information
.TP
.B \-\-home HOME
Instance home directory; omitted siblings default under it; defaults to
~/pavedb
.TP
.B \-\-config CONFIG
Explicit config.yml path; default comes from PAVEDB_CONFIG/config search
.TP
.B \-\-tenants TENANTS
Explicit tenants.yml path; default comes from
PAVEDB_AUTH__TENANTS_FILE/config
.TP
.B \-\-data\-dir DATA_DIR
Explicit data directory; default comes from PAVEDB_DATA_DIR/config
.SH COMMANDS
.SS help
Show help for the CLI or a named command.
.PP
.nf
pavecli help [\-h] [command ...]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B command
Command path to describe
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli help
pavecli help search
pavecli help admin show\-key
.fi
.SS init
Create config.yml, tenants.yml, and the data directory for an instance.
.PP
.nf
pavecli init [\-h] [\-\-force] [root]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B root
Instance home directory
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite config and tenants files if they already exist
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli init
pavecli init ~/pavedb\-staging
pavecli \-\-config /etc/pavedb/config.yml \e
  \-\-tenants /var/pavedb/tenants.yml \e
  \-\-data\-dir /var/pavedb/data init
.fi
.SS admin
Show or rotate the local instance admin key.
.PP
.nf
pavecli admin [\-h] {show\-key,rotate\-key} ...
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli admin show\-key
pavecli admin rotate\-key
.fi
.SS admin show\-key
Print the existing admin key without generating one.
.PP
.nf
pavecli admin show\-key [\-h]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli admin show\-key
.fi
.SS admin rotate\-key
Atomically replace the local admin key and print it once.
.PP
.nf
pavecli admin rotate\-key [\-h]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli admin rotate\-key
.fi
.SS create\-collection
Create a collection, optionally with display and embedder configuration.
.PP
.nf
pavecli create\-collection [\-h] [\-\-display\-name DISPLAY_NAME]
                                 [\-\-embedder EMBEDDER]
                                 [\-\-embedder\-type EMBEDDER_TYPE]
                                 [\-\-embed\-model EMBED_MODEL]
                                 [\-\-embedder\-config EMBEDDER_CONFIG]
                                 [\-\-search\-mode {vector,boost,hybrid}]
                                 [\-\-priority\-key PRIORITY_KEY]
                                 [\-\-chunking CHUNKING]
                                 tenant/collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and new collection, e.g. demo/books. The collection slug takes
lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens; must start with a letter or
digit; max 63 chars
.TP
.B \-\-display\-name DISPLAY_NAME
Human\-readable collection label
.TP
.B \-\-embedder EMBEDDER
Configured embedder selector: instance key, type, type:model, or full
vector\-space key
.TP
.B \-\-embedder\-type EMBEDDER_TYPE
Embedder type, such as sbert, openai, or ollama
.TP
.B \-\-embed\-model EMBED_MODEL
Embedding model name
.TP
.B \-\-embedder\-config EMBEDDER_CONFIG
JSON object with embedder\-specific config
.TP
.B \-\-search\-mode {vector,boost,hybrid}
Default ranking mode for searches that name none (vector)
.TP
.B \-\-priority\-key PRIORITY_KEY
Metadata field whose value in [\-1, 1] scales scores by (1 + value);
omitted: prio_boost
.TP
.B \-\-chunking CHUNKING
JSON object, e.g. {"strategy":"fixed","size":800,"overlap":100} or
{"strategy":"none"}; omitted fields take the instance default
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli create\-collection \-\-display\-name "Books" demo/books
.fi
.SS ingest
Preprocess and index a TXT, CSV, or PDF file into a collection.
.PP
.nf
pavecli ingest [\-h] [\-\-docid DOCID] [\-\-metadata METADATA]
                      [\-\-csv\-has\-header {auto,yes,no}]
                      [\-\-csv\-meta\-cols CSV_META_COLS]
                      [\-\-csv\-include\-cols CSV_INCLUDE_COLS]
                      tenant/collection file
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B file
Path to TXT, CSV, or PDF input
.TP
.B \-\-docid DOCID
Stable document ID; defaults from filename when omitted
.TP
.B \-\-metadata METADATA
JSON object attached to the document
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-has\-header {auto,yes,no}
CSV header handling: auto, yes, or no
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-meta\-cols CSV_META_COLS
CSV columns for metadata only (not indexed). Names or 1\-based indices,
comma\-separated
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-include\-cols CSV_INCLUDE_COLS
CSV columns to index. Names or 1\-based indices, comma\-separated.
Defaults to all non\-meta columns
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli ingest \-\-docid book\-1 \-\-metadata '{"lang":"en"}' demo/books ./book.txt
.fi
.SS ingest\-batch
Index a JSON batch of raw\-text documents.
.PP
.nf
pavecli ingest\-batch [\-h] tenant/collection file
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B file
JSON batch file, or \- for stdin
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli ingest\-batch demo/books ./documents.json
pavecli ingest\-batch demo/books \- < documents.json
.fi
.SS ingest\-text
Index one raw\-text document.
.PP
.nf
pavecli ingest\-text [\-h] [\-\-docid DOCID] [\-\-metadata METADATA]
                           tenant/collection text
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B text
Raw text to index
.TP
.B \-\-docid DOCID
Stable document ID; generated when omitted
.TP
.B \-\-metadata METADATA
JSON object attached to the document
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli ingest\-text \-\-docid note\-1 demo/books "Captain Nemo"
.fi
.SS search
Run ranked search over a collection and print the response envelope.
.PP
.nf
pavecli search [\-h] [\-k K] [\-\-mode {vector,boost,hybrid}]
                      [\-\-include\-common] [\-\-filters FILTERS]
                      [\-\-content\-filter CONTENT_FILTER]
                      tenant/collection query
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B query
Natural\-language search query
.TP
.B \-k K
Number of matches to return
.TP
.B \-\-mode {vector,boost,hybrid}
Ranking mode; defaults to the collection's search mode
.TP
.B \-\-include\-common
Include configured common collection results
.TP
.B \-\-filters FILTERS
JSON object, e.g. {"docid":"DOC\-1"}
.TP
.B \-\-content\-filter CONTENT_FILTER
JSON object with op exact, phrase, prefix, or contains and a non\-empty
value
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli search \-k 3 demo/books "captain nemo"
.fi
.SS list\-queries
List logged query IDs, optionally scoped to a tenant or collection.
.PP
.nf
pavecli list\-queries [\-h] [\-\-tenant TENANT] [\-\-collection COLLECTION]
                            [\-\-limit LIMIT] [\-\-offset OFFSET]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-tenant TENANT
Filter by tenant
.TP
.B \-\-collection COLLECTION
Filter by collection
.TP
.B \-\-limit LIMIT
Maximum entries to return
.TP
.B \-\-offset OFFSET
Entries to skip
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli list\-queries \-\-tenant demo \-\-collection books \-\-limit 20
.fi
.SS get\-query
Resolve a query_id through the catalog and print the stored query log
entry.
.PP
.nf
pavecli get\-query [\-h] query_id
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B query_id
Query ID to fetch
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli get\-query 6f7cfd26\-7d7f\-4e5d\-942b\-f2a516f515a6
.fi
.SS replay\-query
Resolve a query_id through the catalog and run the stored query again.
.PP
.nf
pavecli replay\-query [\-h] query_id
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B query_id
Query ID to replay
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli replay\-query 6f7cfd26\-7d7f\-4e5d\-942b\-f2a516f515a6
.fi
.SS list\-documents
Print indexed documents and their collection metadata.
.PP
.nf
pavecli list\-documents [\-h] tenant/collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli list\-documents demo/books
.fi
.SS get\-document
Print document metadata and chunk summary for one document.
.PP
.nf
pavecli get\-document [\-h] tenant/collection docid
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B docid
Document ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli get\-document demo/books book\-1
.fi
.SS list\-chunks
Print chunk metadata for a document without chunk text content.
.PP
.nf
pavecli list\-chunks [\-h] tenant/collection docid
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B docid
Document ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli list\-chunks demo/books book\-1
.fi
.SS get\-chunk
Print metadata for one chunk by record ID.
.PP
.nf
pavecli get\-chunk [\-h] tenant/collection rid
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B rid
Chunk record ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli get\-chunk demo/books book\-1::chunk_0
.fi
.SS get\-chunk\-content
Write one chunk's text content to stdout.
.PP
.nf
pavecli get\-chunk\-content [\-h] tenant/collection rid
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B rid
Chunk record ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli get\-chunk\-content demo/books book\-1::chunk_0
.fi
.SS delete\-collection
Remove a collection, including its local metadata and vector index.
.PP
.nf
pavecli delete\-collection [\-h] tenant/collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli delete\-collection demo/books
.fi
.SS move\-collection
Rename the collection slug and move its catalog/query\-home records.
.PP
.nf
pavecli move\-collection [\-h] tenant/collection tenant/new\-collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and current collection, e.g. demo/old
.TP
.B tenant/new\-collection
Same tenant and the new collection slug: lowercase letters, digits, and
hyphens; must start with a letter or digit; max 63 chars
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli move\-collection demo/old\-books demo/books
.fi
.SS update\-collection
Update collection metadata such as the display name, without re\-
indexing.
.PP
.nf
pavecli update\-collection [\-h] \-\-display\-name DISPLAY_NAME
                                 tenant/collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B \-\-display\-name DISPLAY_NAME
New human\-readable collection label
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli update\-collection \-\-display\-name "Books" demo/books
.fi
.SS delete\-document
Remove one document and its chunks from a collection.
.PP
.nf
pavecli delete\-document [\-h] tenant/collection docid
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B docid
Document ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli delete\-document demo/books book\-1
.fi
.SS dump\-archive
Offline only; stop the server before reading its data directory. With
tenant/collection, writes that collection as a portable archive. Without
it, writes the whole instance; collections that fail validation are left
out and listed under 'skipped', and the command exits non\-zero.
.PP
.nf
pavecli dump\-archive [\-h] [\-\-output OUTPUT] [tenant/collection]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Collection to export; omit for the instance
.TP
.B \-\-output OUTPUT
Destination ZIP file path
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli dump\-archive \-\-output pavedb\-data.zip
pavecli dump\-archive \-\-output books.zip demo/books
.fi
.SS restore\-archive
Offline only; stop the server first. With tenant/collection, creates
that collection from a same\-version collection archive, or with
\-\-replace overwrites the existing one. Without it, replaces the data
directory from an instance archive.
.PP
.nf
pavecli restore\-archive [\-h] [\-\-replace] [tenant/collection] file
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Destination collection; omit for an instance archive
.TP
.B file
Archive zip file, or \- for stdin
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Overwrite an existing collection instead of creating it
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli restore\-archive pavedb\-data.zip
pavecli restore\-archive demo/books books.zip
pavecli restore\-archive \- < pavedb\-data.zip
.fi
.SS reset\-metrics
Clear the shared runtime metrics in the configured catalog database.
.PP
.nf
pavecli reset\-metrics [\-h]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli reset\-metrics
.fi
.SS list\-tenants
Print tenants currently present in the collection catalog.
.PP
.nf
pavecli list\-tenants [\-h]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli list\-tenants
.fi
.SS list\-embedders
Print configured embedder instances and the resolved default routing
pool.
.PP
.nf
pavecli list\-embedders [\-h] [\-\-tenant TENANT]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-tenant TENANT
Tenant namespace to echo in the response
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli list\-embedders
pavecli list\-embedders \-\-tenant demo
.fi
.SS list\-collections
Print collection names, display labels, and embedder labels for a
tenant.
.PP
.nf
pavecli list\-collections [\-h] tenant
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant
Tenant namespace
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli list\-collections demo
.fi
.SS get\-collection
Print catalog, embedder, vector\-space, document, and chunk details for a
collection.
.PP
.nf
pavecli get\-collection [\-h] tenant/collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli get\-collection demo/books
.fi
.SS reindex
Offline only; start a reindex job and show progress until it finishes.
Ctrl\-C pauses the job after its current batch.
.PP
.nf
pavecli reindex [\-h] [\-\-embedder EMBEDDER]
                       [\-\-embedder\-type EMBEDDER_TYPE]
                       [\-\-embed\-model EMBED_MODEL]
                       [\-\-embedder\-config EMBEDDER_CONFIG]
                       tenant/collection
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B tenant/collection
Tenant and collection, e.g. demo/books
.TP
.B \-\-embedder EMBEDDER
Configured embedder selector for the new vector space
.TP
.B \-\-embedder\-type EMBEDDER_TYPE
Target embedder type
.TP
.B \-\-embed\-model EMBED_MODEL
Target embedding model
.TP
.B \-\-embedder\-config EMBEDDER_CONFIG
JSON object with target embedder settings
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli reindex \-\-embedder v2 demo/books
.fi
.SS reindex\-status
Show durable reindex progress, or list all retained jobs.
.PP
.nf
pavecli reindex\-status [\-h] [job_id]
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B job_id
Reindex job ID
.PP
Examples:
.nf
pavecli reindex\-status
pavecli reindex\-status JOB_ID
.fi
.SS reindex\-resume
Resume reindexing from the persisted staged index and follow progress
until it finishes. Ctrl\-C pauses the job.
.PP
.nf
pavecli reindex\-resume [\-h] job_id
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B job_id
Reindex job ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli reindex\-resume JOB_ID
.fi
.SS reindex\-cancel
Cancel the job and discard its staged vectors.
.PP
.nf
pavecli reindex\-cancel [\-h] job_id
.fi
.PP
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.TP
.B job_id
Reindex job ID
.PP
Example:
.nf
pavecli reindex\-cancel JOB_ID
.fi
.SH PRE-1.0 NOTE
Runtime selectors (\-\-home, \-\-config, \-\-tenants, \-\-data\-dir) are global options.
.br
Pass them before the command, e.g. pavecli \-\-home ./instance list\-tenants.
.br
Store commands open the local data directory directly.
.br
They refuse to run while another PaveDB process owns it.
